<title>PERU: Peru's January cotton output falls 63 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's January cotton output falls 63 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's January cotton production falls 63 percent to 1,001 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Imports of cotton fell in January 20.1 percent to $2.22 million, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>According to the ministry's latest figures, exports of cotton in December rose 5.4 percent to $3.855 million and exports in 1996 rose 24.3 percent to $30.236 million.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
